[17592186097790 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096845 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097874 #edb/ref 1064 "Sometimes, we need to combine multiple rules of differentiation to differentiate a given function. As a reminder, the product rule, quotient rule, and chain rule are stated below.\n\n- Product rule: $\\hspace{.5cm} \\dfrac{\\mathrm{d} }{\\mathrm{d}x } \\left[ u(x) \\cdot v(x) \\right] = u'(x) \\cdot v(x) + u(x) \\cdot v'(x)$\n\n- Quotient rule: $\\hspace{.5cm} \\dfrac{\\mathrm{d} }{\\mathrm{d}x } \\left[ \\dfrac{u(x)}{v(x)} \\right] = \\dfrac{u'(x)\\cdot v(x) - u(x)\\cdot v'(x)}{[v(x)]^2}$\n\n- Chain rule: $\\hspace{.5cm} \\dfrac{\\mathrm{d} }{\\mathrm{d}x } \\left[ u(v(x)) \\right] = u'(v(x))\\cdot v'(x)$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097874 #edb/ref 1065 420 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097874 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "a5d21aee-bc36-5838-871b-9e5a1f7876c3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097874 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233662 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2400" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233662 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233662 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${y}^{'}$ for $y=\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}({x}^{3})}{{x}^{3}+2}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233662 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8304b514-754e-54d2-b053-31a4e39c33dd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186233662 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=\\operatorname{ln}({x}^{3})$ and the denominator $v(x)={x}^{3}+2.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{'}(x)=\\frac{3}{x},\\,{v}^{'}(x)=3{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{'}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{'}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{'}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{3}{x})({x}^{3}+2)-(\\operatorname{ln}({x}^{3}))(3{x}^{2})}{({x}^{3}+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3({x}^{3}+2)-3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}({x}^{3})}{x({x}^{3}+2)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{3}-3{x}^{3}\\operatorname{ln}({x}^{3})+6}{x({x}^{3}+2)^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288034 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{x-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{4{x}^{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288034 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288034 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "018421ea-dca9-5daf-ab3a-c27696ce4249" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288223 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288223 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288223 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "1e02db35-b595-59ea-973e-bd157371128c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288693 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1+2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{2{x}^{2}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288693 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186288693 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "5e5c0bc2-0072-5944-8dd3-fe8dcbae8938" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289177 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289177 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289177 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ac81cfb0-7259-5f57-9adb-04296e897ae4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289380 #edb/ref 1080 "\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-2}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289380 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186289380 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "cb7a7d1a-20e3-5bd6-9408-f184d8d4065a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288034 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288223 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186288693 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290238 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186289380 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290238 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290238 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290238 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186289177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290238 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f45efbdd-39dd-5ca7-b621-baab9c7920f2" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290522 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186290238 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290522 #edb/ref 1069 "q-2403" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290522 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290522 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${y}^{′}$ for $y=\\frac{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{2x}.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290522 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c3d7d091-4a85-557a-b384-1cb4715f620a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186290522 #edb/ref 1074 "We use the quotient rule with the numerator $u(x)=\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}$ and the denominator $v(x)=2x.$ \n\nDifferentiating $u(x)$ and $v(x),$ we have\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}},\\,{v}^{′}(x)=2.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $u.$\n\nNow, applying the quotient rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′}=\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{1}{2x\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}})(2x)-(\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x})(2)}{(2x)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}-2\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{4{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}{4{x}^{2}\\sqrt{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}.\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360974 #edb/ref 1080 "-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360974 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186360974 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "2089f74f-7bb1-531f-9f54-4e2969f07e4d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [175921