7592186362370 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "25941eb3-76ad-51ee-8456-c5400a4c8aea" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186362370 #edb/ref 1074 "To find the slope at a given point, we have to find $\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}$ at that point.\n\nThis question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)={sin}^{3}⁡x.$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2x)({sin}^{3}⁡x)+({x}^{2})(3{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x) \\\\  & =2x{sin}^{3}⁡x+3{x}^{2}{sin}^{2}⁡x\\operatorname{cos}⁡x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the slope at $x=0$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x})|}_{x=0} & =2\\cdot 0\\cdot {sin}^{3}⁡(0)+3\\cdot {0}^{2}\\cdot {sin}^{2}⁡(0)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0) \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186428106 #edb/ref 1030 0.5 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186428106 #edb/ref 1032 "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account foundations: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: foundations=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/foundations-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1115->280. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." #edb/ref 17592186045436] [1