 $f^{′}(x)$ when $f(x) = \\cos^{3} 4x$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489390 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0b547b24-9888-53eb-ab95-e124d3f31432" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489390 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=u^3,\\,u=\\cos v,\\,v=4x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=3u^2,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}=-\\sin v,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}=4.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\\n&=3u^2\\cdot (-\\sin v)\\cdot 4\\\\\n&=-12\\cos^{2} 4x\\sin 4x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489392 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489424 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489392 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489392 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{′}(x)$ when $f(x)={sin}^{3}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489392 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2168b13d-cc27-5e92-a481-beee5381eccc" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489392 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{3},\\,u=\\operatorname{sin}⁡v,\\,v=1{x}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=3{u}^{2},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2x.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡v)\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =3(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1))^{2}\\cdot (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1))\\cdot 2x \\\\  & =6x{sin}^{2}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1{x}^{2}-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [1759218