#edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489427 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $f^{′}(x)$ when $f(x) = \\sin^{3} 2x$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489427 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "b67a6cf9-dc23-5ea7-a514-a5dcfabdbd86" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489427 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=u^3,\\,u=\\sin v,\\,v=2x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=3u^2,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}=\\cos v,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\\n&=3u^2\\cdot (\\cos v)\\cdot 2\\\\\n&=6\\sin^{2} 2x\\cos 2x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489430 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489402 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489430 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489430 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ when $f(x)={cot}^{4}⁡(2x-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489430 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c3baed33-1cfd-5982-8e88-c33747aa34cf" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489430 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,v=2x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-{csc}^{2}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=2.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡v)\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(2x-1))^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(2x-1))\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =-8{cot}^{3}⁡(2x-1){csc}^{2}⁡(2x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${f}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-8{cot}^{3}⁡(2(0)-1){csc}^{2}⁡(2(0)-1) \\\\  & =-8{cot}^{3}⁡(-1){csc}^{2}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =-8(-{cot}^{3}⁡1){csc}^{2}⁡1 \\\\  & =8{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489432 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489450 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489432 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489432 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ when $f(x)={cot}^{4}⁡(3x-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489432 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c51262c0-6413-5083-b852-6971681819a1" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489432 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,v=3x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-{csc}^{2}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=3.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡v)\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(3x-1))^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(3x-1))\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =-12{cot}^{3}⁡(3x-1){csc}^{2}⁡(3x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${f}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-12{cot}^{3}⁡(3(0)-1){csc}^{2}⁡(3(0)-1) \\\\  & =-12{cot}^{3}⁡(-1){csc}^{2}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =-12(-{cot}^{3}⁡1){csc}^{2}⁡1 \\\\  & =12{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489445 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489412 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489445 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489445 #edb/ref 1071 "Find $f^{′}(x)$ when $f(x) = \\cos^{3} 5x$." #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489445 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e7f20887-76fb-5d13-bcfc-20da4d07fad6" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489445 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf=u^3,\\,u=\\cos v,\\,v=5x.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}=3u^2,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}=-\\sin v,\\quad \\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}=5.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f'(x)&=\\frac{\\mathrm{d}f}{\\mathrm{d}u}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}u}{\\mathrm{d}v}\\cdot\\frac{\\mathrm{d}v}{\\mathrm{d}x}\\\\\n&=3u^2\\cdot (-\\sin v)\\cdot 5\\\\\n&=-15\\cos^{2} 5x\\sin 5x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489448 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489400 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489448 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489448 #edb/ref 1071 "Find ${f}^{′}(0)$ when $f(x)={cot}^{4}⁡(1x-1).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489448 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "f751f15c-49b5-572a-960c-e6e9fe0fd73f" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489448 #edb/ref 1074 "First, we express $f$ as the composite function\n\n$$\nf={u}^{4},\\,u=\\operatorname{cot}⁡v,\\,v=1x-1.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}=4{u}^{3},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}=-{csc}^{2}⁡v,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x}=1.\n$$\n\nApplying now the chain rule twice, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}u}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}v}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}v}{\\text{d}x} \\\\  & =4{u}^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡v)\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =4(\\operatorname{cot}⁡(1x-1))^{3}\\cdot (-{csc}^{2}⁡(1x-1))\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =-4{cot}^{3}⁡(1x-1){csc}^{2}⁡(1x-1)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow we compute ${f}^{′}(0):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(0) & =-4{cot}^{3}⁡(1(0)-1){csc}^{2}⁡(1(0)-1) \\\\  & =-4{cot}^{3}⁡(-1){csc}^{2}⁡(-1) \\\\  & =-4(-{cot}^{3}⁡1){csc}^{2}⁡1 \\\\  & =4{cot}^{3}⁡1{csc}^{2}⁡1\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489452 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186096742.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489452 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "9bf95cfb-a852-5313-852a-6ed5187445e3" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489455 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186489459 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489455 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489455 #edb/ref 1071 "If $f(x)={x}^{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x+5),$ find ${f}^{′}(x).$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489455 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "13151117-2915-58a7-8af2-4dc4a9478503" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489455 #edb/ref 1074 "This question requires the product rule. Let $u(x)={x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x+5).$ Then\n\n$$\n{u}^{′}(x)=2x,\\,{v}^{′}(x)=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x+5).\n$$\n\nNote that we used the chain rule to differentiate $v.$\n\nNow, applying the product rule and simplifying, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & ={u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)+u(x)\\cdot {v}^{′}(x) \\\\  & =(2x)(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x+5))+({x}^{2})(6\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x+5)) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡(6x+5)+6{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x+5).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489461 #edb/ref 1168 "generate/scratch/17592186096845.py" #edb/ref 17592186045443] [17592186489461 #edb/ref 1169 #uuid "c8ef6baf-f8d3-5c68-84d8-ed19f665eb6d" #edb/ref 17592186045443]}
